@startuml Blood Stock Management System - Context Diagram (DFD Level 0)

' Styling
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam rectangle {
    BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    BorderColor #1976D2
    FontSize 12
    FontStyle bold
}
skinparam actor {
    BackgroundColor #FFF9C4
    BorderColor #F57C00
}
skinparam arrow {
    Color #424242
    FontSize 10
}

title Blood Stock Management System\nContext Diagram (DFD Level 0)

' External Entities
actor "Donor" as donor #LightYellow
actor "Staff" as staff #LightGreen
actor "Admin" as admin #LightCoral
actor "Recipient" as recipient #LightBlue

' Main System
rectangle "Blood Stock\nManagement\nSystem" as system #E3F2FD {
}

' Data Flows from Donor
donor -down-> system : Registration Details
donor -down-> system : Donation Information
donor -down-> system : Event Registration
donor -down-> system : Location Data
system -up-> donor : Donation Confirmation
system -up-> donor : Certificate
system -up-> donor : Event Details
system -up-> donor : Eligibility Status

' Data Flows from Staff
staff -right-> system : Donor Records
staff -right-> system : Blood Pack Details
staff -right-> system : Donation Records
staff -right-> system : Issuance Information
staff -right-> system : Event Data
system -left-> staff : Inventory Reports
system -left-> staff : Donor Lists
system -left-> staff : Stock Alerts
system -left-> staff : Issuance Receipts

' Data Flows from Admin
admin -down-> system : User Management Data
admin -down-> system : System Configuration
admin -down-> system : Report Requests
system -up-> admin : System Reports
system -up-> admin : Analytics Data
system -up-> admin : User Activity Logs
system -up-> admin : Stock Statistics

' Data Flows from Recipient
recipient -left-> system : Blood Request
recipient -left-> system : Recipient Details
system -right-> recipient : Blood Availability
system -right-> recipient : Issuance Receipt
system -right-> recipient : Blood Pack Information

note right of system
  <b>Central System</b>
  Manages all blood bank
  operations including:
  • Donor Management
  • Inventory Tracking
  • Blood Distribution
  • Event Coordination
  • Certificate Generation
end note

note bottom of system
  <b>Context Diagram</b>
  Shows the system boundary and
  external entities interacting
  with the Blood Stock Management System
end note

@enduml
